window.docContents[59].resolve({"/ISO-80000-11-___-Characteristic-numbers/Dimension-does-not-classify_SEMI_-the-measurement-principle-does/#PropertyKindCalculus-Blueprint--ISO-80000-11-___-Characteristic-numbers--Dimension-does-not-classify_SEMI_-the-measurement-principle-does":{"contents":"\n\nThe dimension-one collision, on the standard — total, the widest in the series. There\nexist distinct ISO 80000-11 kinds with the same dimension one — the Reynolds and Euler\nnumbers witness it, alongside all 113 others. No dimension-only type system can separate\nany two characteristic numbers; the kind layer, through the measurement principle (R2),\nholds the entire part apart. This is dimension does not classify the kind (R1) at its\nabsolute limit. Uses the dimension map and the\nexamination principle.\n\niso80000_11_dim_one_collision : ∃ a b : DimensionedKind, a.kind ≠ b.kind ∧ a.dim = b.dim\n∧ a.dim = 1, witnessed by ⟨reynolds, euler, reynolds_ne_euler, rfl, rfl⟩. Axiom-free.\n\n","context":"PropertyKindCalculus Blueprint\u0009ISO 80000-11 — Characteristic numbers","header":"22.3. Dimension does not classify; the measurement principle does","id":"/ISO-80000-11-___-Characteristic-numbers/Dimension-does-not-classify_SEMI_-the-measurement-principle-does/#PropertyKindCalculus-Blueprint--ISO-80000-11-___-Characteristic-numbers--Dimension-does-not-classify_SEMI_-the-measurement-principle-does"}});